## 3. The Logic of Fractal Binary

**Classical Binary:**  
\[
A \lor \neg A \quad \text{(Either A or not A)}
\]

**Organic Binary:**  
\[
A \land \neg A \quad \text{(Both A and not A, integrated)}
\]

**Fractal Binary:**  
\[
\mathcal{F}_b(A) = \mathcal{F}_b(A \lor \neg A) \land \mathcal{F}_b(A \land \neg A)
\]

The opposition itself is nested within the integration, which is nested within the opposition, which is nested within the integration...

The structure is *self-similar* at every scale.

